# Avoid `useEffect` (Veyra)

Borrowed from Acensure’s developer guide. If you think you need `useEffect`, **ask the user first**.

## Prefer instead

| Goal | Do this |
| :--- | :--- |
| React to a click / submit / dialog close | Event handler |
| Load server data | TanStack Query (when API exists) |
| Derive UI from props/state | Compute during render (`useMemo` only if needed) |
| Form defaults after load | `form.reset(...)` / defaultValues |
| Read localStorage once | Lazy `useState(() => read…())` |
| Write localStorage | Inside the same handler that changes state |
| Flash feedback | `ShowToast` in the handler — not an effect |

## Rare OK cases (still ask)

- Subscribing to `window` / `matchMedia` / third-party widgets with cleanup
- Syncing a non-React library (map, chart imperative API)

## Bad smell

```tsx
// ❌ syncing state from other state
useEffect(() => { setB(a + 1) }, [a])

// ❌ fetch in effect when Query exists
useEffect(() => { fetch(...).then(setData) }, [])
```
